SesAnt is a remix of the open-source projects below. Files derived from them
were changed (generated, cut, scaled and combined by the scripts in cad/scripts/;
the READMEs describe each derivation) and keep the terms of their sources.
The full licence texts are in licenses/.

RealAnt (https://github.com/OteRobotics/realant)
    Copyright (c) 2020 Ote Robotics Ltd, Aalto University
    MIT License -- licenses/realant-MIT.txt
    Used: the body_v6 plate outline and the leg_v8 blade-leg outline (from its
    STLs) for the v1 chassis and blade feet; its serial protocol (sN / meas),
    which the SesAnt firmware implements.

Sesame (https://github.com/dorianborian/sesame-robot)
    Copyright Dorian Todd
    Apache License 2.0 -- licenses/sesame-robot-Apache-2.0.txt
    Used: the internal frame (cut to the spine), foot servo clamps, bottom
    cover, femurs and servo positions from its STL / STEP files; its electronics
    and servo layout.

StackChan (https://github.com/m5stack/StackChan)
    Copyright (c) 2026 M5Stack Technology CO LTD
    MIT License -- licenses/stackchan-MIT.txt
    Used: no StackChan files. SesAnt uses the M5Stack CoreS3 dimensions and, for
    the v3 neck, StackChan's choice of SCS0009 servos, their IDs and step size.

Jumper (https://github.com/KingKongRobotics/jumper)
    Jumper
    Copyright 2026 KingKong Robotics.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 -- licenses/jumper-Apache-2.0.txt
    Used: the claw outline (palm and finger), projected from Jumper's URDF
    meshes, for the SesAnt Jumper jaws; the layout of its task registry, which the
    sesant.flat training task follows. No Jumper files are included; the
    third-party material listed in Jumper's own NOTICE (mjlab, rsl_rl, ...) is
    not included here either. sesant_jumper/sim/install_into_jumper.sh adds the SesAnt
    task to a Jumper checkout that the user obtains separately.

The sesant.flat environment config (sesant_jumper/sim/jumper_tasks/) follows mjlab's
Unitree Go1 velocity task (https://github.com/mujocolab/mjlab, Apache License
2.0), which it imports at run time.

